 ("8.3","Cross-week / carry-forward inventory documented","Flag","SHPX215082 is only partially drawn down this week (offloads 1-2; offloads 3-4 already claimed on the W2 sheet, cited via Ops Notes formula H15 as 19,123.43872 + 19,731.252 = 38,854.69072 kg). No double-counting risk: this week only claims the 2 offloads that occurred within it, and the H15 cell comment cross-references the exact W2 figures being carried forward. HOWEVER, the Ops Notes H15 cell comment itself flags an unresolved, disclosed methodology question: per-BOL ticket evidence places the PHYSICAL unload of all 4 SHPX215082 loads in one continuous ~26.5-hour operation (2026-08-05 14:17 to 2026-08-06 16:52), meaning offloads 1-2 (claimed this week, W3) and offloads 3-4 (claimed on W2) may have physically occurred together, with the week-of-reporting split driven by a COBB bulk-applied injection_completion_date rather than by physical unload timing. Ops team's own open item, tracked internally (their ref 'Claude-m8t') — not a mass or Net CDR error, but an unresolved reporting-period assignment question worth surfacing to Max/Garrett rather than silently passing. [log:ops_notes.section1_railcars_received] [log:_derived_values.ops_notes_h15_w2_carryforward_detail]","VR Sec 3.5"),
 ("8.4","Rail uncertainty conservatism (N offloads at least N inbound BOLs per railcar)","Pass","SHPX215068, SHPX215078, GPRX5082, GPRX5098, GPRX5139 (all FULL, closed this week): each has 4 offloads against 3 inbound BOLs -- conservative. SHPX215082: across its full draw-down (2 offloads on W2 plus 2 offloads on W3, 4 total) against 3 inbound BOLs -- still conservative at the full-railcar level once both weekly batches are combined. [log:ops_notes.section1_railcars_received] [log:_derived_values.shpx215082_n_offloads_combined] [log:_derived_values.shpx215082_n_bols]","Isometric Standard S3.7.3"),

 ("9. Isometric Certify — Removal Component Mapping","","SECTION","",""),
 ("9.1","Sequestration matches internal gross","Pass","Mass of Injectant 417,675.03274 kg x Carbon Content 40.60% x 3.667 = 621.8354 t = Certify Injection Sequestration 621.835 t exactly (see 7.1). This item confirms Certify's reported figure matches what the REPORTED mass produces -- it does not by itself resolve whether the reported mass is correct. See 2.3/2.5: one offload's mass input (GPRX5139 offload_1) is flagged as ~398 kg too high per Charm's own substitution policy, worth ~0.59 tCO2e against this 621.835 t gross if corrected -- immaterial at the whole-removal level (~0.1%) but a genuine, quantified overstatement at the offload level. [log:certify_components.component_modal_reads] [log:_derived_values.gross_co2e_recalc_note] [log:ops_notes.tractor_trailer_check_full_results.mismatch_detail]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.2","Transport: process + embodied per leg (6 components), full math shown","Flag","Arithmetic reconciles exactly for all 6 components using the SINGLE-LEG distances (not the weekly Aggregate/Allocated distance figures, which are the embodied-calc inputs only -- see note below) -- see item 3.5 for a real, separate finding: the Allocated/Aggregate Distance datapoints feeding the embodied side of these calculations are not attached to the Ops Notes (only to route-map images), so the allocation math itself is not independently reconstructable from Certify's attached evidence.\nAECN->SOPOR Truck Process: 424.10852t x 107.49722mi (single-leg) x 0.0001143 MTCO2e/(t-mi) = 5.2110t = Certify 5.211t exactly.\nSOPOR->Opelousas Rail Process: 424.10852t x 2,199mi (single-leg) x 0.000025910374 MTCO2e/(t-mi) = 24.1644t = Certify 24.164t exactly.\nOpelousas->Basco Truck Process: 424.10852t x 42.9mi (single-leg) x 0.0001143 MTCO2e/(t-mi) = 2.0796t = Certify 2.080t exactly.\nAECN->SOPOR Truck Embodied 0.418t, SOPOR->Opelousas Rail Embodied 0.377t, Opelousas->Basco Truck Embodied 0.448t: these DO use the weekly Aggregate/Allocated distance figures directly (1,759.12 / 12,099.05 / 1,887.60mi) x the per-mile embodied EF (0.23756 kgCO2e/mi tanker; 0.0193 kgCO2e/km railcar) with no mass-of-load datapoint (correct -- embodied is per-mile, independent of cargo mass). [log:certify_components.component_modal_reads] [log:certify_datapoints] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_aecn_sopor_recalc_t] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_aecn_sopor_recalc_note] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_rail_recalc_t] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_rail_recalc_note] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_opel_basco_recalc_t] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_opel_basco_recalc_note]\nBio-oil transport total = 5.211+24.164+2.080 (process, 31.455t) + 0.418+0.377+0.448 (embodied, 1.243t) = 32.698t = Certify 'Bio-oil transport' subtotal exactly. [log:certify_components.transport_process_aecn_sopor_t] [log:certify_components.transport_process_sum_t] [log:certify_components.transport_embodied_sum_t] [log:certify_components.transport_total_t] [log:_derived_values.transport_process_sum_t] [log:_derived_values.transport_embodied_sum_t] [log:_derived_values.transport_total_t] [log:standard_ef_sheet_live_check]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.3","Injection: LCS / sample transport","N/A","AECN requires no LCS pre-treatment at Basco; no LCS component on this entry. [log:oil_type]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.4","Pyrolysis: process + embodied present, full math shown","Pass","AECN pyrolysis (from rail loads) - process emissions: 424.10852t x 0.1371171 = 58.153t = Certify exactly.\nAECN pyrolysis (from rail loads) - embodied emissions: 424.10852t x 0.02116 = 8.974t = Certify exactly.\nMass basis = pre-sparging Bio-Oil Mass - AECN via Rail (424,108.52 kg), correct per methodology (6.6). Rail-batch naming ('from rail loads') is the deliberate VVB signal per convention. [log:certify_components.pyrolysis_process_t] [log:certify_components.pyrolysis_embodied_t]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.5","Reductions: applicable BCU categories populated","Fail","Certify's Components tree for this removal contains ONLY 'Stored' (621.835t) and 'Emitted' (99.825t) -- there is NO 'Reductions' category at all, and none of the 19 Certify Sources is a BCU/RD-EAC certificate. Checked the 'Charm EAC Verification Inventory tracker' directly to rule out inventory exhaustion: the RD-EACs retirement certificate (13-47206-50000) carries 2,561.71 units of remaining, undrawn BCU inventory -- well above the 200-unit alert floor and more than sufficient to cover this removal's 31.455t transport-process shortfall. This is the same unexplained BCU-application gap flagged on the prior weekly batch INJ-08-2026-W1 (also zero BCU, also ample inventory available) -- now a 2-for-2 pattern across weekly time-block batches, worth escalating as a systemic gap in the weekly-batch workflow rather than a one-off. [log:certify_components._primary_source_opened] [log:eac_inventory_check.conclusion] [log:eac_inventory_check.total_attributes_remaining]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.6","BCU quantity must at least cover the corresponding transport process activity emission","Fail","Transport process sum = 5.211 + 24.164 + 2.080 = 31.455 t. BCU coverage = 0 t (see 9.5). Shortfall = 31.455 t (100% of transport process emissions unoffset). [log:certify_components.transport_process_aecn_sopor_t] [log:certify_components.transport_process_sum_t] [log:_derived_values.bcu_coverage_t] [log:_derived_values.bcu_shortfall_t]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.7","Counterfactuals zero per protocol","Pass","No counterfactual emission component present on this removal; bio-oil geological storage counterfactual is zero per protocol. [log:certify_components._primary_source_opened]","Certify Components"),
 ("9.8","Net removal matches internal calculation","Pass","Independent recompute 621.835 - 99.824 - 3.460 = 518.551 t = Certify Net CO2e Removed exactly. This arithmetic does not depend on the missing-BCU finding (9.5/9.6) -- Net CDR is correctly stated for what Certify currently reports. [log:certify_calculation_view.recompute_check]","Certify Calculation View"),
 ("9.9","Descriptive source filenames","Flag","Of 19 Certify Sources, several carry non-descriptive or repeated-generic filenames: 'image (44).png' (linked to the SOPOR-Opelousas rail allocated distance), and 5 separate uploads all named identically 'Aug-16-2026-distance-route_map.png' (plus 1 more 'Jul-28-2026-distance-route_map.png') across the 3 aggregate/allocated distance datapoints -- content correct, naming and potential-duplicate-upload pattern only. Same hygiene class as flagged on every sister AECN weekly/rail batch this reporting period. [log:certify_sources_enumeration]","Certify Datapoints"),
 ("9.10","Sources match Drive / complete set","Pass","19 sources enumerated in full from the Certify Sources tab (single source of truth). Every source needed for this removal's 15 datapoints is present: Ops Notes, lab CoA, 3 AECN LCA/GHG period files, 2 EF reference files, and 7 distance/route-map images. No separate per-batch Drive folder holds mass-chain evidence for this removal -- consistent with the weekly-batch convention where Ops Notes hyperlinks are the primary chain of custody. [log:certify_sources_enumeration] [log:certify_sources_tab_total]","Certify Sources"),
]

wb = openpyxl.Workbook()
ws = wb.active
ws.title = "QA Checklist"
ws.append(["Item","Check","Status","Notes / Evidence","Verifier Ref"])
for c in ws[1]:
    c.font = BOLD; c.fill = HEADER_FILL; c.alignment = WRAP; c.border = BORDER
for (a,b,status,*rest) in ROWS:
    ev = rest[0] if rest else ""
    vr = rest[1] if len(rest)>1 else ""
    if status == "SECTION":
        ws.append([a,b,"","",""])
        r = ws.max_row
        for col in range(1,6):
            cell = ws.cell(r,col); cell.fill = HEADER_FILL; cell.font = BOLD; cell.alignment = WRAP; cell.border=BORDER
        continue
    ws.append([a,b,status,ev,vr])
    r = ws.max_row
    for col in range(1,6):
        ws.cell(r,col).alignment = WRAP; ws.cell(r,col).border = BORDER
    if status == "Fail":
        for col in range(1,6): ws.cell(r,col).fill = FAIL_FILL
    elif status == "Flag":
        for col in range(1,6): ws.cell(r,col).fill = FLAG_FILL; ws.cell(r,col).font = FLAG_FONT
    elif status == "N/A":
        for col in range(1,6): ws.cell(r,col).font = NA_FONT
ws.column_dimensions["A"].width = 10
ws.column_dimensions["B"].width = 40
ws.column_dimensions["C"].width = 8
ws.column_dimensions["D"].width = 100
ws.column_dimensions["E"].width = 22

